{
  "category": "Sky Squirrel Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The energy made in its cheeks’ electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "It glides on its outstretched membrane while shocking foes with the electricity stored in the pouches on its cheeks.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It glides on its outstretched membrane while shocking foes with the electricity stored in the pouches on its cheeks.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The energy made in its cheeks’ electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "They live on treetops and glide using the inside of a cape-like membrane while discharging electricity.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "The energy made in its cheeks’ electric pouches is stored inside its membrane and released while it is gliding.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It glides using its cape-like membrane. Electrical energy scatters from it, shocking its friends and foes alike.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It grills berries and bug Pokémon with electric shocks and makes a meal of them. It usually nests in the holes gouged in trees by Pikipek.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "They store up electricity to fly through the air. When thunder cracks at night, sometimes there are almost enough of them to blot out the sky.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "As it flies, it scatters electricity around, so bird Pokémon keep their distance. That’s why Emolga can keep all its food to itself.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "As Emolga flutters through the air, it crackles with electricity. This Pokémon is cute, but it can cause a lot of trouble.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon absolutely loves sweet berries. Sometimes it stuffs its cheeks full of so much food that it can’t fly properly.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
